# Pairwise allowlist for scripts/lint-parallel-pub-types.py.
#
# Format:
#   <TypeName> <crate-a> <crate-b>  # why this duplicate is intentional
#
# Keep entries specific. A type duplicated across three crates needs three
# pair lines only if all three pairs are intentional.

RetryPolicy argo-mcp-connector-shared argo-vertical  # runtime connector retry vs declarative vertical manifest retry

# codex-type-canonicalization-wave-3 — justified-different-concept duplicates.
# Each pair below is intentional; see brief notes for rationale.

# StopReason — three different stop-state vocabularies that happen to share a
# name. argo-cli/work_loop is the worker-loop's TaskComplete/ApprovalRequired/
# NeedInfo/MaxSteps state. argo-executor-computer-use is the CU loop's
# Success/Failure signal. argo-provider is the LLM transport's
# EndTurn/ToolUse/MaxTokens/ContentFilter. Domains are unrelated; merging
# would conflate orthogonal vocabularies.
StopReason argo-cli argo-executor-computer-use
StopReason argo-cli argo-provider
StopReason argo-executor-computer-use argo-provider

# ToolSchema — argo-provider holds the wire-shape projected to LLM providers
# (JSON Schema with provider-side fields); argo-tool holds the tool-registry's
# internal schema record. Same fields today but different boundaries; callers
# already alias one to avoid ambiguity (see ProviderToolSchema in
# argo-agent-runner/src/dispatch.rs).
ToolSchema argo-provider argo-tool

# Workflow — argo-vertical is the declarative manifest schema (TOML
# deserialisation target with `schema_version`, `[[step]]` arrays).
# argo-workflow is the runtime DAG (`tasks`, `edges`, topo-sort target).
# Different shapes, different lifecycles; the vertical manifest compiles
# INTO the DAG, they are not interchangeable.
Workflow argo-vertical argo-workflow

# WorkerResourceConfig — argo-config exposes the operator-facing
# `[worker.resource_cage]` TOML section; argo-runtime exposes the cgroup-v2
# `WorkerResourceCage::install_on` input. Fields are intentionally mirrored
# so operators can override defaults via TOML. A future refactor moves both
# behind a single argo-types definition; tracked in the build-plan, not in
# this brief.
WorkerResourceConfig argo-config argo-runtime

# PrincipalOverride — argo-memory's flag (`UserProtected` lock override) and
# argo-skill's flag mirror each other deliberately so the two stores honour
# the same Agent/Force vocabulary without cross-crate dependency. Folding
# would require adding a dep; the doc comment in argo-skill explicitly
# notes the mirror.
PrincipalOverride argo-memory argo-skill

# StripeClient — deliberate mirror across two architectural layers.
# argo-billing's StripeClient is the internal HTTP client driven by webhook
# delivery + invoice reconciliation (server-to-server, secret-key auth).
# argo-mcp-connector-stripe's StripeClient is the MCP-connector tool-call
# client surfaced to verticals (tenant-scoped credentials, tool schema).
# Different lifecycle, different auth surface, different audit trail; folding
# would conflate billing-trust with tool-call-trust.
StripeClient argo-billing argo-mcp-connector-stripe

# fix-parallel-pub-types-gate-enforce (2026-06-10) — adjudicated the 6 live
# duplicates ahead of flipping gate 4 to --enforce. The two Track-P pairs
# (PitchChannel, CanonicalQaIndex) were genuine duplicates and were
# canonicalized in code, not allowlisted. The four below share only a generic
# name; each pair is a different concept in a different domain.

# ListQuery — argo-bluebubbles-client's is the iMessage-bridge REST list query
# (limit/offset/include for a remote HTTP API). argo-store's is the
# notifications-table pagination cursor (limit/before/exclude_dismissed over
# SQLite). Different fields, different transport, no shared lifecycle.
ListQuery argo-bluebubbles-client argo-store

# SourceKind — argo-cli's (pub(super)) is the worker-overview KPI provenance
# (Messages/ToolCalls/Pending/AnyAction/NotComputable). argo-genesis's is the
# onboarding-intake modality (Document/Voice/Image/WikiUrl). Unrelated
# vocabularies; folding would conflate KPI plumbing with intake ingestion.
SourceKind argo-cli argo-genesis

# StepOutcome — argo-cli's (pub(super)) is a workflow-step UI blob
# ({status,message} strings for the wizard). argo-orchestrator's is the
# settled team-run step result ({step_id, status: StepStatus, output}).
# Different shapes, different layers (presentation vs orchestration).
StepOutcome argo-cli argo-orchestrator

# StepStatus — argo-cli's is the setup-checklist status (Ok/Fail/Skip).
# argo-orchestrator's is the delegation-step lifecycle
# (Completed/Failed/Skipped). Different state machines that happen to share a
# name; merging would couple readiness checks to the run-graph executor.
StepStatus argo-cli argo-orchestrator

# CuRiskTier — identical copy-paste of the executor-floor reversibility enum
# (Observe/Act) across the per-platform CU executor crates. cfg-gated, mutually
# exclusive compilation. ALLOWLISTED rather than canonicalized because the
# Windows crate cannot be compile-verified on macOS; a proper canonicalization
# into the shared base crate (argo-executor-computer-use) is queued for the
# Windows fleet.
CuRiskTier argo-executor-computer-use-macos argo-executor-computer-use-windows
